1
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:07,080
[Fragments of Truth]

2
00:01:07,080 --> 00:01:08,640
[Episode 5]

3
00:01:16,760 --> 00:01:17,070
Hello?

4
00:01:18,070 --> 00:01:18,920
The police are onto me.

5
00:01:19,230 --> 00:01:20,400
What did they want?

6
00:01:20,680 --> 00:01:21,590
Did you say anything?

7
00:01:22,280 --> 00:01:23,710
I didn't say a word.

8
00:01:23,710 --> 00:01:25,840
But they might come back for me.

9
00:01:25,840 --> 00:01:28,680
So get me out right now.

10
00:01:29,760 --> 00:01:30,560
Abroad...

11
00:01:30,560 --> 00:01:31,150
Abroad. Yes, exactly.

12
00:01:31,150 --> 00:01:31,710
Abroad.

13
00:01:31,710 --> 00:01:32,640
Get me out of the country now.

14
00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:35,150
I'll find you a place to hide first.

15
00:01:35,150 --> 00:01:36,070
I can't wait.

16
00:01:36,480 --> 00:01:37,680
I can't wait another day.

17
00:01:38,680 --> 00:01:40,480
Don't push me.

18
00:01:40,480 --> 00:01:40,920
Push me too far,

19
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:42,040
and I'll spill everything.

20
00:01:42,040 --> 00:01:43,350
I'll just go back to prison.

21
00:01:43,350 --> 00:01:44,200
At least

22
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:45,950
I'd be safer there, right?

23
00:01:46,070 --> 00:01:47,280
Do you really have to be this scared?

24
00:01:47,870 --> 00:01:48,480
I am.

25
00:01:49,070 --> 00:01:49,760
Do you get it?

26
00:01:49,760 --> 00:01:52,920
Do you know who killed
Dongzi and Lao Zou?

27
00:01:53,760 --> 00:01:54,070
Who?

28
00:01:57,950 --> 00:01:58,870
Xiao Ting.

29
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:01,200
She is still alive.

30
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:04,920
She came back for revenge.

31
00:02:09,430 --> 00:02:11,710
Her elderly father first
reported her missing.

32
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:14,680
But Xiao Ting was an adult.

33
00:02:15,030 --> 00:02:17,520
There was no evidence she was in danger.

34
00:02:18,150 --> 00:02:19,710
It dragged on for months

35
00:02:19,710 --> 00:02:20,910
before the case could be opened.

36
00:02:21,750 --> 00:02:23,960
Then her mother fell ill.

37
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:25,240
She couldn't afford treatment.

38
00:02:25,750 --> 00:02:26,910
She died within days.

39
00:02:27,590 --> 00:02:28,000
Sighs.

40
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:30,080
Two months later, her father died too.

41
00:02:31,430 --> 00:02:33,430
He died clutching the family register,

42
00:02:33,430 --> 00:02:36,360
asking a nurse if his daughter was back.

43
00:02:37,470 --> 00:02:39,240
Did you keep investigating
her disappearance?

44
00:02:39,430 --> 00:02:39,910
We did.

45
00:02:40,430 --> 00:02:43,030
No travel, phone, or bank records.

46
00:02:43,710 --> 00:02:44,280
Right.

47
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:45,280
She was somewhere in the city,

48
00:02:45,280 --> 00:02:46,520
with no steady job,

49
00:02:46,520 --> 00:02:47,750
so we had no way to trace her.

50
00:02:48,150 --> 00:02:49,840
We could only issue
an assistance notice.

51
00:02:50,710 --> 00:02:51,870
That's just how these cases go.

52
00:02:52,560 --> 00:02:54,030
Especially out here near the border.

53
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:56,590
Some people are tricked
across the border

54
00:02:56,590 --> 00:02:58,800
and only then learn
they can never return.

55
00:03:01,560 --> 00:03:03,310
Even if we knew where they were,

56
00:03:04,030 --> 00:03:04,870
how could we bring them back?

57
00:03:06,910 --> 00:03:07,960
Up ahead is Wuli Village.

58
00:03:36,630 --> 00:03:37,360
This is her place.

59
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:38,870
No one lives here now.

60
00:03:39,470 --> 00:03:41,150
Most villagers have moved away.

61
00:03:41,280 --> 00:03:42,360
Not just their family.

62
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:44,520
The government planned a relocation.

63
00:03:45,030 --> 00:03:45,560
Watch your head.

64
00:03:46,310 --> 00:03:48,310
They moved several villages together.

65
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:52,310
Careful.

66
00:05:07,430 --> 00:05:08,000
Lao He.

67
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:08,950
Boss.

68
00:06:24,430 --> 00:06:25,270
Han Ning.

69
00:06:25,600 --> 00:06:26,430
What are you doing?

70
00:06:27,040 --> 00:06:28,310
The case pressure's getting to you.

71
00:06:29,870 --> 00:06:31,160
What do you think?

72
00:06:31,240 --> 00:06:33,390
Do you really think the
suspect is Xiao Ting?

73
00:06:34,830 --> 00:06:37,870
So our detective whiz
has another theory?

74
00:06:38,680 --> 00:06:38,870
No.

75
00:06:39,510 --> 00:06:40,720
I found something.

76
00:06:41,560 --> 00:06:42,000
Look.

77
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:46,070
This is footage from our pinhole camera.

78
00:06:46,360 --> 00:06:48,830
Traffic cameras also caught the suspect.

79
00:06:51,070 --> 00:06:52,270
Before the murder,

80
00:06:52,750 --> 00:06:54,950
the suspect walked very slowly.

81
00:06:55,190 --> 00:06:56,000
Their center of gravity was high.

82
00:06:56,510 --> 00:06:57,920
Their arms swung widely too.

83
00:06:58,920 --> 00:06:59,310
Yeah.

84
00:07:02,830 --> 00:07:03,870
But after the murder,

85
00:07:04,190 --> 00:07:05,190
their center of gravity was lower.

86
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:08,390
Their arm swing was much smaller too.

87
00:07:09,070 --> 00:07:09,510
Like this.

88
00:07:11,480 --> 00:07:12,630
That difference is very strange.

89
00:07:13,560 --> 00:07:14,510
You have to understand,

90
00:07:14,950 --> 00:07:17,040
after committing the murder,

91
00:07:17,040 --> 00:07:19,270
the killer would've
been extremely tense.

92
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:22,750
Their normal gait should
be hard to alter.

93
00:07:23,750 --> 00:07:25,720
The killer had just taken a life.

94
00:07:25,870 --> 00:07:27,480
However cold-blooded they were,

95
00:07:27,870 --> 00:07:29,830
taking a life with his own hands

96
00:07:29,950 --> 00:07:31,630
would cause psychological trauma.

97
00:07:31,750 --> 00:07:33,950
A physical stress response is normal.

98
00:07:34,430 --> 00:07:34,750
Right.

99
00:07:35,830 --> 00:07:36,630
There's another possibility.

100
00:07:37,720 --> 00:07:41,040
The killer may be skilled at evasion.

101
00:07:41,040 --> 00:07:43,270
He deliberately altered his posture

102
00:07:43,510 --> 00:07:44,600
to fool

103
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:47,040
cameras and eyewitnesses.

104
00:07:48,720 --> 00:07:50,160
I understand your reasoning.

105
00:07:51,070 --> 00:07:53,560
But could there be another explanation?

106
00:08:10,480 --> 00:08:12,680
I have a question for you, Ms. Ding.

107
00:08:13,310 --> 00:08:13,870
I'm listening.

108
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:14,630
Go ahead.

109
00:08:15,750 --> 00:08:16,870
When might someone suddenly change

110
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:19,750
their posture and habitual movements?

111
00:08:20,430 --> 00:08:22,120
Something like a split personality?

112
00:08:24,310 --> 00:08:25,720
Do you know about behavioral baselines?

113
00:08:29,360 --> 00:08:29,680
Yeah.

114
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,720
A person's usual behavior patterns

115
00:08:31,720 --> 00:08:33,670
and physical habits.

116
00:08:33,720 --> 00:08:36,120
Does leaving that baseline only mean

117
00:08:36,510 --> 00:08:37,840
a change in mood, or posture too?

118
00:08:38,720 --> 00:08:40,080
Let me give you an imperfect example.

119
00:08:40,270 --> 00:08:43,030
Say a hunched beggar puts on a fine suit

120
00:08:43,270 --> 00:08:44,630
and enters a wealthy man's party.

121
00:08:45,240 --> 00:08:47,870
They'll likely smile, glass in hand,

122
00:08:48,200 --> 00:08:49,200
standing tall with their head up.

123
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:51,360
In other words,

124
00:08:51,480 --> 00:08:52,600
if someone's behavior doesn't match

125
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:54,320
their usual identity,

126
00:08:54,750 --> 00:08:56,150
they must be experiencing something

127
00:08:56,150 --> 00:08:57,440
far outside the norm.

128
00:08:59,270 --> 00:09:01,960
Far, far outside the norm.

129
00:09:02,750 --> 00:09:04,270
Only when the difference is great enough

130
00:09:04,320 --> 00:09:05,600
and the impact strong enough

131
00:09:06,270 --> 00:09:09,510
can years of habitual movement

132
00:09:09,870 --> 00:09:10,390
be altered.

133
00:09:16,270 --> 00:09:17,870
And the greater the change,

134
00:09:18,080 --> 00:09:19,000
the greater the impact.

135
00:09:21,080 --> 00:09:23,320
Enough to make them
seem like two people.

136
00:09:52,200 --> 00:09:53,320
Ever heard of transformation makeup?

137
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:54,440
Transformation makeup?

138
00:09:54,960 --> 00:09:56,320
It's essentially a disguise.

139
00:09:57,030 --> 00:09:59,030
Some people are exceptionally skilled

140
00:10:00,080 --> 00:10:02,390
at making themselves
look like celebrities.

141
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:05,080
You can barely tell
without a close look.

142
00:10:28,600 --> 00:10:29,600
So that's it.

143
00:10:36,960 --> 00:10:37,720
Found you.

144
00:10:42,320 --> 00:10:45,640
[Donglin City Public Security Bureau
Criminal Investigation Detachment]

145
00:10:47,510 --> 00:10:48,440
Captain, Uncle He.

146
00:10:48,670 --> 00:10:48,910
Hey!

147
00:10:49,360 --> 00:10:50,360
Go get two cups of water.

148
00:10:50,360 --> 00:10:50,630
Yes.

149
00:10:51,960 --> 00:10:52,840
Mix in some cold water.

150
00:10:52,840 --> 00:10:53,360
Sure thing.

151
00:10:55,870 --> 00:10:57,240
Captain Ren, what's this?

152
00:10:57,550 --> 00:10:58,910
Xiao Ting and her parents.

153
00:11:00,030 --> 00:11:00,870
Why is there a boy in the photo?

154
00:11:01,390 --> 00:11:02,200
Where's Han Ning?

155
00:11:02,870 --> 00:11:03,870
Haven't seen him all day.

156
00:11:03,870 --> 00:11:04,910
He didn't say where he was going.

157
00:11:05,600 --> 00:11:07,000
No discipline. Tell him to come back.

158
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:08,440
Wait, I know!

159
00:11:08,550 --> 00:11:10,790
I know how the killer avoided detection.

160
00:11:13,840 --> 00:11:15,200
Drink slowly.

161
00:11:15,670 --> 00:11:16,120
Hey.

162
00:11:16,870 --> 00:11:17,270
We

163
00:11:17,600 --> 00:11:19,360
were wrong from the start.

164
00:11:19,600 --> 00:11:21,080
We assumed the killer was a woman.

165
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:21,790
Actually,

166
00:11:21,790 --> 00:11:23,030
the killer is Xiao Ting's brother,

167
00:11:23,510 --> 00:11:24,600
Jiang Li.

168
00:11:26,080 --> 00:11:26,910
How did you figure that out?

169
00:11:27,360 --> 00:11:29,320
I visited Xiao Ting's home village.

170
00:11:29,670 --> 00:11:31,510
Her brother was born when she was two.

171
00:11:31,670 --> 00:11:32,870
Money was tight.

172
00:11:33,360 --> 00:11:36,120
Her parents gave her
to a distant cousin.

173
00:11:36,510 --> 00:11:38,960
Once they had a son, they gave her away.

174
00:11:39,670 --> 00:11:41,360
So police records showed

175
00:11:41,670 --> 00:11:43,510
no link between Xiao Ting and Jiang Li.

176
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:44,790
But they

177
00:11:45,550 --> 00:11:46,630
were actually siblings.

178
00:11:47,320 --> 00:11:47,550
Yes.

179
00:11:48,790 --> 00:11:50,670
Very few knew that.

180
00:11:51,720 --> 00:11:52,510
Let's take a look.

181
00:11:53,360 --> 00:11:55,750
Jiang Li and Xiao Ting
resemble each other.

182
00:11:56,120 --> 00:11:58,870
Jiang Li studied makeup in school.

183
00:11:59,240 --> 00:12:01,000
So the Xiao Ting we saw

184
00:12:01,200 --> 00:12:03,510
was Jiang Li in disguise.

185
00:12:06,270 --> 00:12:09,790
Our investigation was
off from the start.

186
00:12:13,320 --> 00:12:14,870
That can't be right.

187
00:12:14,870 --> 00:12:15,910
Wouldn't people notice?

188
00:12:16,670 --> 00:12:17,870
He's a master of cross-dressing.

189
00:12:17,870 --> 00:12:20,510
He can look more feminine than a woman.

190
00:12:20,840 --> 00:12:21,600
More feminine than you?

191
00:12:22,870 --> 00:12:23,480
Then

192
00:12:23,480 --> 00:12:25,120
everything starts to make sense.

193
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:28,440
Xiao Ting died by suicide.

194
00:12:28,840 --> 00:12:30,840
Zou Jun and Xu Haodong were involved.

195
00:12:32,510 --> 00:12:34,030
To avenge his sister,

196
00:12:34,390 --> 00:12:37,360
Jiang Li disguised himself as a woman
to approach Zou Jun.

197
00:12:38,320 --> 00:12:39,960
After subduing him,

198
00:12:41,670 --> 00:12:43,320
he made himself look like his sister

199
00:12:43,670 --> 00:12:44,960
so Zou Jun would see Xiao Ting

200
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:47,120
and be terrified.

201
00:12:47,720 --> 00:12:48,870
It was as if Xiao Ting

202
00:12:49,240 --> 00:12:50,120
herself

203
00:12:50,750 --> 00:12:51,960
had taken revenge.

204
00:12:53,150 --> 00:12:55,480
If Yu Hongfei was telling the truth

205
00:12:55,480 --> 00:12:57,480
and Xiao Ting died by suicide,

206
00:12:57,910 --> 00:13:01,910
what did Zou Jun and Xu Haodong do

207
00:13:01,910 --> 00:13:03,080
to make Jiang Li hate them so much?

208
00:13:03,080 --> 00:13:05,240
No one knows where her body is.

209
00:13:06,550 --> 00:13:07,670
And why did Jiang Li

210
00:13:07,790 --> 00:13:10,200
wait seven years to take revenge?

211
00:13:11,080 --> 00:13:13,360
We need Jiang Li to answer all of this.

212
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:02,960
[Time Post Office]
[To Jiang Li, seven years later]

213
00:14:07,600 --> 00:14:11,960
[Time Post Office]

214
00:14:18,150 --> 00:14:18,600
Sis.

215
00:14:19,150 --> 00:14:19,960
What are you writing?

216
00:14:20,360 --> 00:14:21,200
No peeking.

217
00:14:22,510 --> 00:14:23,440
Be good and write your letter.

218
00:14:24,120 --> 00:14:25,200
Let me just look once.

219
00:14:32,640 --> 00:14:35,480
[Time Post Office]
[To Jiang Li, seven years later]

220
00:15:17,110 --> 00:15:19,180
♪I stand in a fire-tempered jungle♪

221
00:15:19,180 --> 00:15:21,120
♪Withered leaves fall
as my strength runs dry♪

222
00:15:21,120 --> 00:15:23,030
♪Dust swirls as I clench my fists♪

223
00:15:23,030 --> 00:15:24,840
♪I strategize, my faith my armor♪

224
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:27,170
♪My defiance spills onto concrete♪

225
00:15:27,170 --> 00:15:29,600
♪Even thick fog can't hide
my clear gaze♪

226
00:15:32,740 --> 00:15:34,650
♪Let neon turn to thorns♪

227
00:15:34,650 --> 00:15:36,550
♪Flying low as the stars shift and turn♪

228
00:15:36,550 --> 00:15:38,490
♪Escape the maze,
transcend the challenge♪

229
00:15:38,490 --> 00:15:40,620
♪The meter starts, breaking the silence♪

230
00:15:40,650 --> 00:15:42,630
♪A beam cuts through
a crack in the wall♪

231
00:15:42,630 --> 00:15:44,790
♪This rhythm and noise
echo through the streets♪

232
00:15:48,380 --> 00:15:51,860
♪Don't be afraid. No one will answer♪

233
00:15:51,860 --> 00:15:55,230
♪Why is that child crying?♪

234
00:15:55,460 --> 00:15:57,930
♪The shrinking scar on my arm♪

235
00:15:57,930 --> 00:15:59,550
♪Means I've grown up♪

236
00:15:59,550 --> 00:16:02,700
♪You can trust me when I say that♪

237
00:16:02,700 --> 00:16:06,180
♪The wound still aches♪

238
00:16:06,590 --> 00:16:10,940
♪Like a biting winter♪

239
00:16:10,940 --> 00:16:14,210
♪But a spark still glows♪

